221;||on||||||&#8221; body_text_align=&#8221;center&#8221; body_text_color=&#8221;#000000&#8243; body_font_size=&#8221;20px&#8221; background_color=&#8221;rgba(0,0,0,0)&#8221; background_enable_color=&#8221;on&#8221; transform_scale_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_translate_phone=&#8221;0px|-138px&#8221; transform_translate_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_rotate_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_skew_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_origin_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_styles_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; background_layout=&#8221;light&#8221; global_colors_info=&#8221;{}&#8221; sticky_transition=&#8221;on&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>Thank you for making Bnos Yisroel such an amazing, creative, innovative, patient, and warm hearted place to learn, through pandemics and tweenagers. I sincerely bentch you that HKB\u201dH should continue to give you the kochos to endure and to persist in reaching every one of your talmidos and may you share incredible nachas from every single one, knowing your direct impact.&#8221;<\/p>\n<p><em>- S. Waitzman, High School parent<\/em><\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_slide][et_pb_slide admin_title=&#8221;Kaplowitz&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.16&#8243; body_font=&#8221;||on||||||&#8221; body_text_align=&#8221;center&#8221; body_text_color=&#8221;#000000&#8243; body_font_size=&#8221;20px&#8221; background_color=&#8221;rgba(0,0,0,0)&#8221; background_enable_color=&#8221;on&#8221; transform_scale_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_translate_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_translate_linked_phone=&#8221;off&#8221; transform_rotate_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_skew_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_origin_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_styles_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; background_layout=&#8221;light&#8221; global_colors_info=&#8221;{}&#8221; sticky_transition=&#8221;on&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>\u201cI have taught in many Jewish schools all over the United States. Right from the beginning, it was evident that the administration at Bnos Yisroel respects and supports its teachers\u2026Mrs. Itzkowitz and Mrs. Heyman are very open to new ideas and show a great degree of flexibility so that we teachers can work with them to expand the program\u2026<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/bnosyisroel.org\/testimonials\/\"><em>Read More&#8230;<\/em><\/a><\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_slide][et_pb_slide admin_title=&#8221;To Mrs. Fine&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.16&#8243; body_font=&#8221;||on||||||&#8221; body_text_align=&#8221;center&#8221; body_text_color=&#8221;#000000&#8243; body_font_size=&#8221;20px&#8221; background_color=&#8221;rgba(0,0,0,0)&#8221; background_enable_color=&#8221;on&#8221; transform_scale_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_translate_phone=&#8221;0px|-138px&#8221; transform_translate_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_rotate_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_skew_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_origin_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_styles_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; background_layout=&#8221;light&#8221; global_colors_info=&#8221;{}&#8221; sticky_transition=&#8221;on&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>&#8220;To me, leaving home in the morning and dropping her off at school has always been equal to - leaving home\u2026\u2026 and dropping her off at her other home. A home where I knew she was literally enveloped in love, care, safety, concern for her wellbeing\u2026. knowing that when she went off to school, she was being watched by people who would show the same amount of care that I would&#8230;<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/bnosyisroel.org\/testimonials\/\"><em>Read More&#8230;<\/em><\/a><\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_slide][et_pb_slide admin_title=&#8221;New Student Feedback&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.16&#8243; body_font=&#8221;||on||||||&#8221; body_text_align=&#8221;center&#8221; body_text_color=&#8221;#000000&#8243; body_font_size=&#8221;20px&#8221; background_color=&#8221;rgba(0,0,0,0)&#8221; background_enable_color=&#8221;on&#8221; transform_scale_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_translate_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_translate_linked_phone=&#8221;off&#8221; transform_rotate_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_skew_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_origin_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; transform_styles_last_edited=&#8221;off|phone&#8221; background_layout=&#8221;light&#8221; global_colors_info=&#8221;{}&#8221; sticky_transition=&#8221;on&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p>All of you are so devoted and dedicated to raising happy children who are ovdei Hashem and really believe in themselves which is a rarity.<\/p>\n<p><em>- An Elementary School Parent<\/em><\/p>\n<p>\u2026From my Maalot students, I am constantly impressed by my Bnos students who have such good middos and they believe in themselves and Hashem.<\/p>\n<p><em>-A Maalot Teacher<\/em><em><\/em><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/bnosyisroel.org\/testimonials\/\"><em>Read More&#8230;<\/em><\/a><\/p>\n<p>[\/et_pb_slide][\/et_pb_slider][\/et_pb_column][\/et_pb_row][\/et_pb_section][et_pb_section fb_built=&#8221;1&#8243; inner_shadow=&#8221;on&#8221; custom_padding_last_edited=&#8221;on|desktop&#8221; prev_background_color=&#8221;#ffffff&#8221; admin_label=&#8221;section&#8221; _builder_version=&#8221;4.16.1&#8243; background_enable_color=&#8221;off&#8221; use_background_color_gradient=&#8221;on&#8221; background_color_gradient_type=&#8221;elliptical&#8221; background_color_gradient_stops=&#8221;#ffffff 0%|#dacce5 100%&#8221; background_color_gradient_start=&#8221;#dacce5&#8243; background_color_gradient_end=&#8221;#ffffff&#8221; background_enable_image=&#8221;off&#8221; background_position=&#8221;bottom_center&#8221; background_enable_pattern_style=&#8221;on&#8221; background_pattern_style=&#8221;tufted&#8221; background_pattern_color=&#8221;rgba(255,255,255,0.47)&#8221; background_pattern_size=&#8221;custom